# 8.dogfood.reminder

## .what

prove the RouteReminder daemon delivers its nudge end to end, against rhachet 1.47.6 —
whose `clone say` now reports a mid-turn message as `enqueued` (a SUCCESS verdict) rather
than a false `MalfunctionError`.

## .why

the prior dogfood stone (`7.dogfood`) proved the daemon's own crash-loud self-exit design
held up correctly under an UPSTREAM `clone say` defect, reported as `ehmpathy/rhachet#527`.
that defect is fixed upstream in rhachet 1.47.6 (PR #548), which gave `clone say` a screen
read channel over the input triple and six verdicts — `enqueued` among them, as a success.

so the one path `7.dogfood` could NOT prove — a CLEAN tick delivery into a live session —
is provable now. this stone proves it, and closes the loop on the reported defect.

## .done when

- a daemon is registered for this session via `route.reminder.gen`, on auto-derived flags
- `route.reminder.get` reports the reminder live, with a real pid that answers `kill -0`
- a tick delivers the nudge into THIS session, observed as a real injected input
- that tick writes NO crash log — the delivery is clean, not a tolerated fault
- `route.reminder.del` deregisters it cleanly, with no orphan pid left on the host
- the `sayToClone` exit-code contract is re-read against the new six-verdict CLI, and any
  mismatch is either fixed or recorded as a named follow-up
